  "runtimeScope": [
    "Carry unresolved update_item/remove_item receipts through acknowledgement, HTTP error, empty message, iteration limit and thrown transport errors in rejectedCartEdits.",
    "Retain tool, product and source-line ownership. Successful retries clear their own rejected edit. A mistaken numeric index can recover when the original owner remains the sole projected owner.",
    "Protect earlier rejections when another variant or a newly added copy is edited. Repeating a removal of an already removed accepted source does not invent a rejection. A later invalid update still remains unresolved.",
    "Hold the complete mixed action plan in the router, ahead of nested attribute clarification. Explain controlled reasons and persist the existing clarification marker to protect checkout.",
    "Reuse existing full-reformulation and explicit-decline followups, cart reminders and confirmation gate. The prompt requests clarification of the complete plan after any unresolved replacement/update/removal."
  ],
  "developmentFindings": [
    "The initial20-case run failed17 checks on the previous runtime. Sixteen mixed requests were not owned by the router after a rejected edit, and a variant-owner rejection was absent from the agent result. All provider calls and order operations were simulated.",
    "The expanded successful-recovery fixtures initially used the checkout placedOrderOnly entry, whose established contract ignores successful proposed cart edits. They were corrected to the building-cart edit entry, then completed normal checkout and asserted a single mocked closure.",
    "Review of recovery ownership found that a newly added copy could otherwise clear the rejection of the sole original SKU. Projected owners are captured before each edit. Two extra controls protect new-copy ownership and a missing-owner update after an earlier successful update."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "Provider responses, Meta, persistence, map quotes and order creation are simulated. Real-model wording and representative pilot outcomes require further measurement.",
    "An accepted numeric owner proposed by the model still requires broader validation against the customer phrase, especially with multiple variants. This batch preserves rejection ownership after the tool declines an edit.",
    "Recovery through a different tool, partial correction replay and ambiguous selections may still require a complete reformulation or explicit decline.",
    "Production promotion and generic Kamppo adaptation remain pending."
  ],
